1
00:00:04,739 --> 00:00:08,059
Chapter nine

2
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:20,159
I believe that for his escape he took advantage of the migration of a flock of wild birds.

3
00:00:20,159 --> 00:00:25,139
On the morning of his departure he put his planet in perfect order.

4
00:00:25,139 --> 00:00:30,000
He carefully cleaned out his active volcanoes. He possessed two active

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,920
volcanoes; and they were very convenient for heating his breakfast in the morning.

6
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:38,460
He also had one volcano that was extinct.

7
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:42,960
But, as he said, "One never knows!"

8
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:46,739
So he cleaned out the extinct volcano, too.

9
00:00:46,739 --> 00:00:54,239
If they are very well cleaned out, volcanoes burn slowly and steadily, without any eruptions.

10
00:00:54,239 --> 00:00:58,440
Volcanic eruptions are like fires in a chimney.

11
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:03,300
On our earth we're obviously much too small to clean out our volcanoes.

12
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:08,219
That is why they bring no end of trouble upon us.

13
00:01:08,219 --> 00:01:12,719
The little prince also pulled up, with a certain sense of dejection,

14
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:20,880
the last little shoots of the baobabs they believed that he would never want to return.

15
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:27,960
But on this last morning all these familiar tasks seemed very precious to him.

16
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:32,579
And when he watered the flower for the last time, and prepared to place her

17
00:01:32,579 --> 00:01:42,619
under the shelter of her glass globe, he realized that he was very close to tears.

18
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:51,440
"Goodbye," he said to the flower.

19
00:01:51,599 --> 00:01:54,980
But she made no answer.

20
00:01:56,579 --> 00:02:01,079
"Goodbye," he said again.

21
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:03,059
The flower coughed.

22
00:02:03,059 --> 00:02:06,980
But it was not because she had a cold.

23
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:14,900
"I have been silly," she said to him, at last.

24
00:02:15,659 --> 00:02:19,460
"I ask your forgiveness.

25
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,639
Try to be happy..."

26
00:02:22,739 --> 00:02:26,880
He was surprised by this absence of reproaches.

27
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:32,699
He stood there all bewildered glass globe held arrested in midair

28
00:02:32,699 --> 00:02:38,059
He did not understand this quiet sweetness.

29
00:02:38,818 --> 00:02:43,440
"Of course I love you," the flower said to him.

30
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:47,699
"It is not my fault that you have not known it all the while. That is of no

31
00:02:47,699 --> 00:02:49,079
importance.

32
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:54,539
But you-- you have been just as foolish as I.

33
00:02:54,539 --> 00:02:57,119
Try to be happy...

34
00:02:57,119 --> 00:03:00,300
let the glass globe be.

35
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:08,579
I don't want it anymore But the wind--" "My cult is not so bad as all that...

36
00:03:08,579 --> 00:03:11,400
the cool night air will do me good.

37
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,800
I am a flower."

38
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:22,800
"But the animals--" "Well, I must enjoy the presence of two or three butterflies

39
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:27,300
and the caterpillars if I wish to become acquainted with them

40
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:30,599
It seems that they are very beautiful.

41
00:03:30,599 --> 00:03:35,699
And if not the butterflies-- and the caterpillars-- who will call upon me?

42
00:03:35,699 --> 00:03:38,780
You will be far away...

43
00:03:38,818 --> 00:03:45,059
as for the large animals-- I am not at all afraid of any of them.

44
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:48,420
I have my claws."

45
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:53,818
And naively she showed her four thorns.

46
00:03:53,818 --> 00:04:01,139
Then she added: "Don't linger like this. You have decided to go away.

47
00:04:01,139 --> 00:04:03,780
Now go!"

48
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:08,300
For she did not want him to see her crying.

49
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:13,940
She was such a proud flower
